      <processInformation>
        <referenceFunction amount="1" category="electronics" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="This dataset can be applied to describe the production of an average optical computer mouse. The total weight of the mouse is 0.120 kg. The information is based on weighing carried out at the EMPA labs. Dataset for mouse is compared with the recent inventory data from literature and manufacturers' data. Additionally, it is assumed that energy consumption is decreased during manufacturing stage; UUID: 4d9a8c70-1a23-346b-b843-e5505ddfc329" includedProcesses="Describes the production of a standard optical computer mouse. Calculated per 1 mouse (1 unit). Included are the materials (mainly metals and plastics) with their respective manufacturing processes (e.g. the rolling of the supporting steel plate or the injection moulding of the plastic and rubber for cover, base and wheel). The infrastructure is calculated via the proxy &quot;electronic component factory&quot;. Electricity for the assembly of the optical computer mouse is 4 MJ. The water consumption during production has not been taken into account due to lack of information. The required ship, rail and road transport for input materialsplus the disposal of the computer mouse is part of the dataset." infrastructureIncluded="false" infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="electronics" localName="Mouse device, optical, with cable, at plant" localSubCategory="devices" name="Mouse device, optical, with cable, at plant" subCategory="devices" unit="p"/>
        <geography location="GLO" text="The data is based on weighing measurement at the EMPA Laboratories in 2006. The optical mouse looked at is available all over the world. Therefore a global dataset is justifiable."/>
